window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Twenty years ago teenager Bree Watson had the world at her fingertips. The only thing she was worried about was which Grimlock brother she had the biggest crush on. Then, in a moment of confusion while playing with a Ouija board, she disappeared.<br> <br> Nobody knew what happened to her. Her parents were cleared of suspicion. The girls with her that night didn’t have any answers. She was just gone.<br> <br> And now she’s back.<br> Luna Thorn knows something is very wrong with what happened. Bree went somewhere for twenty years but she came back looking the same, and claiming no time has passed. It’s a miracle…and yet Luna isn’t celebrating with everybody else.<br> <br> Where did Bree go? Was she lost in time? It seems Detroit’s new traveler is on deck to figure it out. If that wasn’t enough, her mother is hanging around Grimlock Manor looking for quality time with her daughter, and she doesn’t seem to be in a hurry to leave.<br> <br> Months ago, Luna’s life was simple. Now things are spiraling. The only question is, just how bad can things get? Can Luna figure out what happened to Bree before the evil that returned with her takes over the city?<br> <br> You’re about to find out…as long as Luna can survive to tell the tale. Buckle up, because this story can only be solved in the past if Luna wants to keep the present safe.</p>"; 
